{"parentUuid":null,"isSidechain":true,"promptId":"df226819-4f0d-4979-bf53-3ffca405c7dd","agentId":"a85a54fd8aba74c8b","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"Repo C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers (live adapter layer in cuore/live/). Python .venv\\Scripts\\python.exe. No subagents, no commits, never open COM3 or call live endpoints (car on the bench, main session owns it); unit tests with the raw reply strings below. Minimal grepping. Report under 100 words. Other agents own cuore/live/ops.py, store.py, dossier_bridge.py, fullscan.py: do not edit; you own cuore/live/obd.py (PID decode table), a new cuore/live/mode09.py if needed, the Mode 06 decoder module (grep -l \"MID\" cuore/live/*.py once; likely mode06.py), and cuore/tests/check_pid_decode.py (new).\n\nTonight's live read of the 2018 Stelvio ECM (18DAF110) showed 46 supported Mode 01 PIDs but cuore decodes only 25; these came back raw and undecoded (reply bytes after \"41 <pid>\"): 13→03, 15→0A 80, 1C→01, 2C→00, 2D→FF, 34→7F 80 80 00, 3C→14 DC, 40→FE D0 90 81, 41→00 04 80 A4, 47→2C, 49→53, 4A→50, 54→EE 15, 59→01 8B, 60→01 21 40 00, 68→03 53 62 00 … (multi-frame), 6B→01 7F 00 00 00, 70→02 00 00 0C … (multi-frame), 72 (read it as the wastegate PID). Implement SAE J1979 decoders for every one of them with the standard formulas (O2 sensor presence bitmap 13; O2 B1S2 voltage + STFT 15; OBD standard 1C with the enum text; commanded EGR 2C; EGR error 2D; O2 wide-range lambda+current 34; catalyst temp B1S1 3C; PIDs supported 41-60 (40), monitor status this drive cycle (41) decoded to the same monitor table readiness uses; absolute throttle B 47; accelerator pedal D/E 49/4A; absolute evap system vapour pressure 54 (kPa, two's complement per spec); fuel rail absolute pressure 59; PIDs supported 61-80 (60); intake air temperature sensors 68 (per bank, the multi-sensor layout from the spec); exhaust gas recirculation temperature 6B; boost pressure control 70 (commanded/actual, per spec sub-fields); wastegate control 72). Each decoded with name, value(s), unit, source \"SAE J1979 (CORROBORATED)\" in the table's docstring. Multi-frame replies must reassemble (the existing reassemble helper). Also: Mode 09: decode PIDs 02 VIN (exists), 04 calibration IDs, 06 CVNs, 0A ECU name, 08 in-use performance tracking (IPT counters per monitor, numerator/denominator — this is the EVAP monitor completion-rate evidence) into a read function other code can call, if ops has none (check ops.read_vin's query pattern; put the decoder in your module and expose decode_mode09(pid, raw_by_ecu)). Mode 06: MID 01 came back \"CAN ERROR\" mid-multi-frame; make the decoder retry a MID once on CAN ERROR and report \"retry failed\" honestly instead of aborting. Tests: every raw string above decodes to the expected numbers (compute them from the formulas and assert), unknown PID still returns raw, Mode 09 04/06/08 decode from synthetic frames, Mode 06 retry path. Run your test plus cuore/tests/check_live.py."},"uuid":"db3dd0e5-1d77-4f3e-9ee1-99f0a4b4e04e","timestamp":"2026-10-14T00:27:03.772Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers","sessionId":"7cb02eb5-e299-4baf-b34b-9eb82aebbf17","version":"2.1.282","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"binary-splashing-comet"}
